 ## Phase B: Fan out
 
 Spawn all N subagents in one message with `run_in_background: true`, each with the task, the path to the shared grounding, its own output path, and instructions to produce both the artifact and a short rationale.
 
+Claude tiers share a lineage, so each seat also gets a stance that pushes it toward a different part of the design space. Append the seat's stance to its prompt. Stances follow seat position in the runners line, not the model, so `opus, opus, opus` still gets three stances.
+
+| Seat | Default model | Stance |
+|------|---------------|--------|
+| 1 | `opus` | Design the end state: the foundational shape this should have if it were built right from the start, even if it moves more code. |
+| 2 | `fable` | Subtract: design the smallest thing that works. Cut every type, layer, and option the task does not force. |
+| 3 | `sonnet` | Design the most conventional fit: match the patterns the codebase already uses, so a maintainer finds nothing surprising. |
+
+Seats past the third get no stance. A stance sets where to push, not what to ignore: each candidate still meets the whole task.
+
 Each rationale names the alternatives the candidate considered and what it rejected.
 
 If a candidate fails to produce output, proceed with N-1 and note the dropout in the synthesis record.
 
 ## Phase C: Cross-judge
 
-After all Phase B candidates complete, choose one model from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in `~/.claude/pstack-models.md`. If the file or that line is missing, choose from `opus`, `fable`, `sonnet`. Prefer a different model family from the parent's. Spawn one readonly judge subagent on that model. It sees the rubric and the candidates by path label, scores each criterion, and recommends a base with rationale. It runs in parallel with the parent's reading in Phase D, not with the candidates themselves. Don't spawn the judge while candidates are still writing.
+After all Phase B candidates complete, choose one model from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in `~/.claude/pstack-models.md`. If the file or that line is missing, choose from `opus`, `fable`, `sonnet`. Prefer a tier other than the parent's. Spawn one judge subagent on that model, with no stance, and tell it not to edit files. It sees the rubric and the candidates by path label, scores each criterion, and recommends a base with rationale. It runs in parallel with the parent's reading in Phase D, not with the candidates themselves. Don't spawn the judge while candidates are still writing.
 
